From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:56:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(effort):=20one=20Effort=20everywhere=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20live,=20Compare,=20Lab=20Book,=20widget,=20fitness?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20age?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The day's Effort with the gym extra (training/VictorDayEffort) reached Today and Trends but not every
reader. Now:

- Fitness Age / VO2max: the scheduled pass adds the extra to its fresh rows, as the "refresh" button's
  merged rows already had it, so the two no longer write different ages for the same week.
- Compare and Lab Book: resolvedSeries("strain") carries the extra.
- Today: the live Effort (ring, tile, chart badge) carries it too, recomputed when an analysis lands;
  the water goal follows the live Effort, as its comment said.
- Widget: its Effort is today's row, never the last scored day's (the carry-over stays for Charge/Rest).
- Banister Effort: the extra is inverted and mapped back with the day's own denominator.
- Means of the day in progress: the coach's 30-day Effort and steps, Trends' Effort mean and move, and the
  week digest skip today's half-day; its point still plots. Trends and Explore re-read with new data.
- Illness heads-up: a hard day is the day BEFORE the judged night with Effort in WHOOP's High band (14/21),
  not two workouts logged today.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
